    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30154" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκατα-λέγω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>build in</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλαὶ στῆλαι
				ἐγκατελέγησαν</span>
			<i>were built into</i> the wall, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.93
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>count</i> or <i>reckon among</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Par.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰς εἰς τοὺς
			Εὐπατρίδας</span>, = Lat. <i>adlegere inter
				patricios</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				43.47
			</span></i>; <i>enlist soldiers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				11.265
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>lie in</i> or <i>on</i>, 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκατέλεκτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.431
				</span></i>
			.</div>
